  [PASS] C2.1 THE REMOVABILITY THRESHOLD, ROUTE 1 (potential propagation).  The twist is a coboundary EXACTLY on the rungs where mu itself descends — SEQ and REC — and on no coarser rung.  At REC the obstruction is zero for the reason C0 gives and for no other: mu is class-constant (ANCHOR AB4.4), so 1/mu is a per-RECORD potential.  At MULT, STATE, PORT and MENU mu is multi-valued and the obstruction is non-zero.  The record functor sits EXACTLY at the threshold — which is a structural explanation of D72's blindness theorem, not a restatement of it  (obstruction (independent cycles + defective self-loops) by rung: SEQ 0, REC 0, MULT 88, STATE 88, PORT 88, MENU 88; mu descends by rung: SEQ 3969/3969, REC 2477/2477, MULT 514/578, STATE 84/125, PORT 24/65, MENU 44/113)
  [PASS] C2.2 THE REMOVABILITY THRESHOLD, ROUTE 2 (relabelled recount — the D64 C7 idiom, adapted to R+).  The spanning-forest potential is propagated over the quotient's OWN up-graph and the entire square census is then RE-RUN with the gauged weights q' = q phi(alpha(h.e))/phi(alpha(h)); the surviving non-unit squares are counted.  Route 2 agrees with route 1 rung for rung: zero survivors exactly where the obstruction is zero  (surviving non-unit squares after the relabelling, by rung: SEQ 0, REC 0, MULT 88, STATE 88, PORT 96, MENU 180)
  [PASS] C2.3 ANTI-VACUITY: the removability test at the coarse rungs is NOT a test on a forest.  The quotient exchange graphs carry independent cycles and/or defective self-loops, so a flat answer was available and was not returned.  (At SEQ the exchange graph is a perfect MATCHING — 1546 edges on 3092 nodes, cycle rank 0 — which is precisely why C0's verdict there carries no information.)  (exchange-graph cycle rank / defective self-loops by rung: SEQ 0/0, REC 145/0, MULT 0/88, STATE 0/88, PORT 80/44, MENU 134/44)
  [PASS] C2.4 THE sigma-PORT RUNG, REPORTED AS THE PIN PREDICTED IT.  D62's sigma machinery at transport scope is the PORT rung: the per-actor option data that the committed weights actually read.  It does NOT carry the whole holonomy — it closes only part of the defective census — so the pin's expectation is upheld, and what does carry it is named in SEC 4  (PORT closes 44 of 88 defective squares (65 classes); MENU closes 44; STATE and MULT close 88 and 88 but at the price of losing descent (C2.1's multi-valued weights: 4 and 8 labelled edges))
  [DATA] TH-C VERDICT (AB4): removable at ['SEQ', 'REC']; NOT removable at ['MULT', 'STATE', 'PORT', 'MENU']
